# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values for local development.
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed — no secret belongs in source
# control, and no value in THIS file is a working credential.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# D-037: an application-owned environment variable is permitted ONLY when the
# value must be known before the database can be read, or when it determines
# where persistent state lives. Everything else is a database-backed setting.
# Adding a variable to this file requires an ADR.
#
# The list below is deliberately short. Session timeouts, the brand name, the
# default locale, the time zone, the maintenance banner — all of those are
# settings in the database (`PlatformSettings.platformConfig`), editable by an
# administrator at runtime, NOT environment variables.
#
# TZ, NODE_ENV, PORT, proxy settings, CA paths and container runtime settings
# are PLATFORM variables, not SplashTrack configuration, and are not listed as
# application config here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Where persistent state lives -------------------------------------------
# The one connection string, shared by the Prisma CLI (prisma.config.ts) and the
# runtime client (src/lib/database/client.ts). There is NO default: a missing or
# wrong value must fail loudly at boot rather than quietly reach the wrong
# database. `docker compose up postgres` starts a local Postgres matching
# docker-compose.yml.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/splashtrack

# --- Must be known before the database can be read --------------------------
# Signs session tokens and encrypts TOTP secrets. Better Auth reads this when
# the auth instance is constructed at module scope — before any database read is
# possible — so it cannot be a setting.
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
# Rotate per deployment. Never reuse a value between environments.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Public base URL of this instance (scheme + host + optional port, no trailing
# slash). Better Auth derives cookie/redirect origins from it, and the WebAuthn
# relying-party id is derived from its host — which is why it cannot be a
# runtime setting: it is read once at auth-context construction.
#
# WARNING (D-132, FM-15): changing the host here changes the WebAuthn RP ID and
# INVALIDATES EVERY EXISTING PASSKEY at once. Moving from a LAN name to a real
# domain is the expected path for this deployment, so set it deliberately.
# Every account keeps a password + TOTP fallback precisely so this is
# recoverable rather than a total lockout.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional: pin the WebAuthn relying-party id explicitly instead of deriving it
# from BETTER_AUTH_URL's host. Use the registrable parent domain when the app is
# served from a subdomain and passkeys should work on both. Same "changing this
# invalidates every passkey" warning applies.
# PASSKEY_RP_ID=

# --- Test harness (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# The vitest suite derives its database from DATABASE_URL by appending `_test`
# to the database name, and refuses to run against anything else. Set this only
# when the test database lives somewhere else entirely (e.g. a CI service
# container). It is subject to the same `_test`-suffix guard.
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=
